Q: How to restrict generic type parameters to a set of classes? A: <p>Note that your types are redundant as <code>string</code> and <code>char[]</code> both implement <code>IEnumerable&lt;char&gt;</code> and <code>byte[]</code> implements <code>IEnumerable&lt;byte&gt;</code>. So you need only two types:  <code>IEnumerable&lt;char&gt;</code> and <code>IEnumerable&lt;byte&gt;</code>.</p>
<p>This means that you have four possible combinations if you allow the conversions between <code>char</code> and <code>byte</code>.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>IEnumerable&lt;char&gt; EncrpytChars(IEnumerable&lt;char&gt; tinSource, ...);
IEnumerable&lt;char&gt; EncrpytChars(IEnumerable&lt;byte&gt; tinSource, ...);
IEnumerable&lt;byte&gt; EncrpytBytes(IEnumerable&lt;char&gt; tinSource, ...);
IEnumerable&lt;byte&gt; EncrpytBytes(IEnumerable&lt;byte&gt; tinSource, ...);
</code></pre>
